## Workflow — 10 phases, 3 human gates, 3 holistic reviews

The same orchestrated SDLC runs on both tools: an **orchestrator** delegates to **planner → developer → reviewer → tester**, with the reviewer additionally running 3 holistic review phases (pre-test, pre-PR, post-PR). All work is sequential within the monorepo.

| Phase | What | Gate |
|---|---|---|
| 1 | Requirements | — |
| 2 | Plan | GATE #1 |
| 3 | Develop (per-task: dev → reviewer) | — |
| 4 | Holistic Pre-Test Review | — |
| 5 | Approval | GATE #2 |
| 6 | Test | — |
| 7 | Holistic Pre-PR Review | — |
| 8 | Architecture & Rules Reconciliation | — |
| 9 | PR Creation | GATE #3 |
| 10 | Holistic PR Review (comment-only) | — |

- **Claude Code**: `/dev-workflow <story-issue-number>` (installed `platform-sdlc-harness` plugin).
- **OpenAI Codex**: invoke the **platform-dev-workflow** skill; it spawns the role subagents and stops at each gate for `APPROVED`.

**Pipeline**: `idea → /discovery-workflow → /backlog-workflow → /dev-workflow → /pr-review`. Discovery shapes an idea into an Epic → Feature → Story tree as GitHub Issues with sub-issue links + board items (planner-only, 3 internal phases). Backlog-workflow refines each Story via Issue body edits + Comments (4 sub-commands: `improve`, `analyze`, `refine`, `enrich`). Dev-workflow implements one Story end-to-end (table above). PR-review is the standalone form of Phase 10.

